Committed on branch `fix/normalize-path-root` (commit `78949d2`).

One small decision the plan didn't specify: I treated a `..` following an already-kept `..` (e.g. `'a/../..'`) as unresolvable and thus preserved it per the relative-path rule, rather than absorbing it at the root. This matches "a relative path keeps every `..` it cannot resolve" and is handled by the `out[out.length - 1] !== '..'` guard — `'a/../..'` → `'..'`, and `'../..'` → `'../..'`.

